# Content, API & Tests

## MDX content

- Source of truth: `content/projects/*.mdx`, `content/blog/*.mdx`.
- Loaders live in `lib/` (no Contentlayer if it fights the toolchain — prefer a typed MDX loader).
- Frontmatter is validated (Zod or equivalent) before render — fail build on bad content.
- No runtime CMS fetches.

## Contact API (`POST /api/contact`)

Pipeline order is fixed:
1. Reject if honeypot filled.
2. Validate body.
3. Rate-limit (Upstash Redis, IP-based).
4. Send via Resend.
5. Return success/error JSON — no stack traces.

## Env vars

- Never commit secrets. Document every required key in `.env.example`.
- Read env only in server code (`lib/` integrations, route handlers).

## Tests (Vitest)

- Unit-test pure `lib/` modules first (validation, rate-limit helpers, loaders).
- RTL for interactive client components when behavior is non-trivial.
- No network calls in unit tests — mock Resend/Upstash.

## SEO (when implementing)

- Every page: title template, description, canonical, OG/Twitter.
- JSON-LD for Person and BlogPosting where specified.
- `sitemap.ts` and `robots.ts` derived from content, not hand-maintained lists.
